Third-party code
================

third_party/fdedge/ is a copy of the FDEdge implementation

    https://github.com/ChangfuXu/FDEdge  (commit 551988866f934b5cdb672e9122279a73eba60259)

released with the paper

    C. Xu et al., "Enhancing QoE in Collaborative Edge Systems With Feedback Diffusion Generative Scheduling,"
    IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing, 2025. doi:10.1109/TMC.2025.3587744

The files are unchanged; only the results/ images of that repository are left out. The FDEdge repository does not
state a license, so its code remains under the copyright of its authors and is not covered by the MIT License in
LICENSE. It is included so that the experiments run against the exact public code. If you are an author of FDEdge and
would like this copy changed or removed, please open an issue.

Code in slot_state/ that builds on FDEdge:
  agents.py       subclasses the FDEdge diffusion actor, replay buffer and agent to switch the feedback input on,
                  and builds the public SAC and DQN baselines with their published hyperparameters
  environment.py  subclasses the public environments to add the state options
  train.py        follows the training loops of fdedge_main.py and baselines/*/*_main.py
